error[E0277]: `HashMap<std::string::String, i64>` is not built from one scalar
  --> tests/ui/scalar_target/map_needs_a_map.rs:11:22
   |
11 |     opens_one_leaf::<HashMap<String, i64>>();
   |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this decrypt target is not a `ScalarTarget`
   |
   = help: the trait `ScalarTarget` is not implemented for `HashMap<std::string::String, i64>`
   = note: a scalar target is a `FromScalar` type, such as `String`, `i64`, or `Vec<u8>`. An `Option` or a `Protected` of one is a scalar target too. So is a newtype that derives `Decrypt` over one.
   = note: a sequence, a map, and a struct with named fields each need a container. So none of them is a scalar target.
   = note: a target with a hand-written sink is a scalar target when that sink implements `TakesScalar`.
note: required by a bound in `opens_one_leaf`
  --> tests/ui/scalar_target/map_needs_a_map.rs:8:22
   |
 8 | fn opens_one_leaf<T: ScalarTarget>() {}
